From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:51:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 563/563] [DS4.1] Grouped MoE GEMM: 2-bit scale codes for
 experts whose block scales span at most 4 values

An expert whose every row's scale deltas fit 2 bits also carries them as
one byte a row (four deltas, low bits first) and a per-expert flag; its
CTAs copy those bytes instead of the 4-bit codes. Every thread expands
its own rows from either form to the uncoded GEMM's scale words, as the
4-bit path does, so the bits are the uncoded GEMM's.
